\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Boundary use versus boundary ontology rendered as a stepwise permission diagram for the no-self-evidence claim. Step 1 shows the shared finite b0-b5 bitstream as the only evidenced object; Step 2 licenses reading those same bits through admissible QRF sector labels for prediction, policy selection, and model comparison when the equal-distribution audit passes; Step 3 blocks treating any chosen sector frame as a real self/world boundary because the perturbation control fails. Color encodes the licensed and blocked lanes, while the legend names the two verdicts, keeping the figure a finite software audit and not empirical, neural, clinical, practice-efficacy, or physical qFEP evidence.}}{5}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
